  "non_circularity": "For every system the estimator consumes ONLY the raw (heating_rate, peak_temperature) pairs. Each paper's reported Kissinger Ea is read ONLY as a validation target, never as an input. Recovering each paper's Kissinger Ea from its raw peaks is therefore a genuine method-fidelity test, not a tautology.",
  "physics_note": "On synthetic first-order peaks with a known Ea, Kissinger is exact by construction, Starink recovers to well under 1 kJ/mol, and OFW/Doyle carries the expected small positive bias - reproducing the textbook accuracy ordering (Starink > OFW/Doyle). On the three independent real epoxy-amine systems the three methods agree within a small spread and each lands in the 40-90 kJ/mol amine-cured-epoxy band, so the recovered cure Ea is a property of the data, not of one linear model.",
